From: Chaz Bailey <charles.s.bailey@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pmic_glink_altmode: do not wait for ack on PAN_ACK

ALTMODE_PAN_ACK (0x11) is an acknowledgement sent by the host to the
firmware. Waiting for an acknowledgement of an acknowledgement is invalid
and causes a 5-second timeout on firmware versions that do not generate
a reply. Make ALTMODE_PAN_ACK fire-and-forget, and do not fail initialization
if ALTMODE_PAN_EN times out.

Signed-off-by: Chaz Bailey <charles.s.bailey@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -164,10 +164,13 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&altmode->pan_ack, 5 * HZ);
+	if (cmd == ALTMODE_PAN_ACK)
+		return 0;
+
+	left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&altmode->pan_ack, 2 * HZ);
 	if (!left) {
-		dev_err(altmode->dev, "timeout waiting for altmode request ack for: %#x\n", cmd);
-		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		dev_warn(altmode->dev, "timeout waiting for altmode request ack for: %#x (continuing)\n", cmd);
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
